  "id": "expressive-suppression",
  "term": "expressive suppression",
  "definition": "Expressive suppression is an emotion regulation strategy in which a person holds back or inhibits the outward display of emotion. In the supplied source, it is contrasted with cognitive reappraisal and is described as often carrying greater psychological costs during stress.",
